{"id":"4685415","name":"Travis Hunter","team":"JAX","pos":"CB","grp":"DEF","num":"12","head":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/nfl/players/full/4685415.png","age":23,"exp":"2","college":"Colorado; Jackson State University","draft":["2025","1","2"],"depth":{"pos":"LCB","rank":1,"unit":"Base 4-3 D","team":"JAX"},"inj":{"status":"Active","note":"The two-way player is beginning to flash the talent that made him the second overall pick in the 2025 NFL Draft. Hunter's receiving numbers were by far a season high -- he had only two catches coming into Sunday -- and his day on offense was capped by a seven-yard touchdown reception from Trevor Lawrence in the fourth quarter that brought the Jaguars to within a field goal at 31-28. Hunter then made an impact on the very next possession, picking off a C.J. Stroud pass in the end zone with just under four minutes left on the clock to keep his team in the game. The touchdown and interception were each the second of his career in his 13th NFL game, and Hunter became the first player since 2002 to have one of each in the same game. Jacksonville's receiver room is crowded with Parker Washington, Jakobi Meyers and Brian Thomas at the top of the depth chart, but head coach Liam Coen hinted after the game that Hunter's role on offense could continue to grow following the team's Week 7 bye, per CBS 47 Jacksonville.","date":"2026-10-18T17:56Z","detail":""},"next":null,"dvp":null,"news":[{"h":"Tracking Jaguars CB/WR Travis Hunter's 2026 season: A career best in Week 6?","d":"Every week, we will look at how many snaps the two-way corner/receiver plays on offense and defense. Is there a trend in his usage?","t":"2026-10-18T21:13:02Z"},{"h":"Travis Hunter stars in Jaguars' loss, is 1st with INT and TD catch since 2002","d":"The Jaguars' Travis Hunter had a historic day at Wembley Stadium, becoming the first player since 2002 to record an interception and TD catch in the same game.","t":"2026-10-18T20:42:10Z"}],"log":[{"s":2026,"w":6,"o":"HO